hey guys merry here with a not-so-great  gamespot news update sounds like  rockstar is delaying GTA 5 for pc again  this is kind of changing the overall  well-known slogan from pc master race2  pc last place for the third time  rockstar has delayed the pc release of  grand theft auto 5 pushing the launch to  april 14 the game was initially  scheduled to ship in fall of 2014 and  then in late january and then on march  24 this third delay pushes the release  back by three more weeks rockstar said  our apologies to PC gamers worldwide who  have been counting down the days until  the launch of our game but a bit more  time is needed to ensure that the game  is as polished as possible as a gesture  of goodwill players who pre-ordered the  game will receive a  two-hundred-thousand-dollar in-game cash  bonus to use in GTA online this brings  the total pre-order bonus to 1.5 million  there's also some good news for the  owners of released versions of GTA 5  because long-awaited heist mode has been  given a launch date of March 10th now  Rockstar said we'll be releasing more  information on heists in the next few  weeks but until then you can check out  the high res screen shots they just  released over at gamespot.com / news
 

